Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 18:31:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 046/154] refactor: AtriumNativeWidgetMac moves to its own file
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

243 lines out of atrium_browser_window.mm. The class turned out to be
self-contained: it holds a Browser and nothing else, and CommandTarget and
InterceptInputs are its OWN private methods rather than the window's. So the
move needed no seam decision and changes no routing.

Exposed as a factory returning views::NativeWidget, so the header names no
platform type and the class stays private to the implementation. Each port
supplies its own file of this shape.

kTitlebarHeight is read from both sides of the split, so it moves to a small
portable header rather than being duplicated.

The move needed seven includes the window had been supplying transitively -
the mojom for CreateWindowParams among them.

Verified by devtools-dock 2 of 2, little-window-hotkey 2 of 2 with two
windows, and sidebar-row-click 3 of 3. Those cover the command dispatcher the
class installs, the window creation params it populates, and the command
routing it decides.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
